senses.gloss:
अधी (√ इ), अध्य्-ए॑ति, or अ॑ध्य्-एति (exceptionally अधीयति, RV. x, 32, 3), to turn the mind towards, observe, understand, RV. & AV.;
 chiefly Ved. (with gen. [cf. Pāṇ. ii, 3, 52] or acc.) to mind, remember, care for, long for, RV. &c.;
to know, know by heart, TS.; ŚBr.; Up. &c.;
to go over, study, MBh. iii, 13689;
to learn from (a teacher's mouth abl.), MBh. iii, 10713;
to declare, teach, ŚBr. x; Up. : Ā. अधीते॑ or (more rarely) अधीयते (Mn. iv, 125; Pot. 3. pl. अधीयीरन्, Kauś.; Mn. x, 1)
to study, learn by heart, read, recite:
Caus. अध्य्-आपयति (aor. -आपिपत्, Pāṇ. ii, 4, 51) to cause to read or study, teach, instruct:
Caus. Desid. अध्य्-आपिप-यिषति, to be desirous of teaching, Pāṇ. ii, 4, 51 :
Desid. अधीषिषति, to be desirous of studying, Pāṇ. viii, 3, 61, Sch.

अधि-√ 1. कृ to place at the head, appoint;
to aim at, regard;
to refer or allude to;
to superintend, be at the head of (loc.), MBh. iv, 241:
Ā. -कुरुते, to be or become entitled to (acc.), MBh. iii, 1345 ;
to be or become superior to, overcome, Pāṇ. i, 3, 33.

अधि-√ 1. क्षि (3. du. -क्षितः॑; 3. pl. -क्षिय॑न्ति)
to be settled in or over, be extended over or along (acc. or loc.), RV.; MBh. i, 722 and 730;
to rest upon, ŚBr.

अधि-√ क्षिप् to throw upon;
to bespatter;
to insult, scold;
to superinduce (disease).

अधि-√ गम् to go up to, approach, overtake;
 to approach for sexual intercourse;
 to fall in with;
 to meet, find, discover, obtain;
to accomplish;
to study, read:
Desid. P. अधि-जिगमिषति, to seek;
 Ā. अधि-जिगांसते, to be desirous of studying or reading.

अधि-√ 1. गा P. to obtain;
 P. (aor. Subj. 2. pl. -गात, or -गातन) to remember, notice, RV. & AV.;
 P. or generally Ā. (-जगे, -अगीष्ट, -अगीष्यत, Pāṇ.) to go over, learn, read, study;
to attempt, resolve:
Caus. P. -गापयति, to cause to go over or teach:
Desid. Caus. -जिगापयिषति, to be desirous of teaching, Pāṇ. ii, 4, 51.

अधि-√ धा (Pass. 3. sg. -धायि, RV.) Ved. to place upon;
to give, share between (dat. or loc.), RV.;
 Ā. (aor. -अधित; perf. -दधे, p. -द॑धान)
to acquire additionally, RV.

अधि-ष्ठा (√ स्था) to stand upon, depend upon;
to inhabit, abide;
to stand over;
to superintend, govern;
to step over or across;
to overcome; to ascend, mount;
to attain, arrive at.
